<Base title="Terms" description="What the published specs are, and what they are not." crumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Terms", href: "/terms/" }]}>
  <h1>Terms</h1>
  <p>
    The pages quote manufacturer documents. They are not the operator’s manual, not a dealer quote, and not an instruction to modify a tractor.
    Specifications change by year, market, and serial number. The document date on each page is the date of that fact.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for confirming a part number and a lift figure against the manual and the parts lookup for your machine before you order or mount anything.
    Rear lift, loader lift, and published weight are not a ballast recipe.
  </p>
  <p>
    The fit check compares published numbers. A result of “inside the published range” means the verified PTO figures sit inside the maker’s printed range and the hitch phrases are compatible under the rules on that page.
    “Cannot tell” means the documents we have do not support a comparison.
  </p>
</Base>
